<description>
Fill black gaps by reconstructing the cyclic symmetric coordinate table visible in the non-black cells.

Input structure:
- The grid is square, with black pixels marking missing cells in an otherwise complete symmetric table.
- The first row is complete: it shows the diagonal color, the previous cycle color, then paired runs of the palette cycle.
- Every non-black input pixel already agrees with the hidden table.

Rule:
- Read the palette cycle from every other first-row cell starting at column 2, stopping when the diagonal color repeats.
- For a cell, let near = min(row, column) and dist = abs(row - column).
- Use the diagonal color when dist is 0, the previous cycle color when dist <= near + 1, otherwise cycle through blocks of width near + 2.

Key insight:
The missing pixels are not locally interpolated; they are entries of a global symmetric table indexed by distance from the main diagonal.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "square grid with black gaps in a symmetric diagonal-index table; the complete first row gives the cyclic palette order",
  "transform": "reconstruct the full table from row and column coordinates: main diagonal uses the first palette color, cells within near+1 of the diagonal use the previous cycle color, and farther cells cycle in blocks of width near+2; fill the black gaps"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 21x21 square
  palette:
    cycle_length: 6-9
    colors: rotation of [1..N], i.e. consecutive integers wrapping around
    diagonal_color: cycle[0] (arbitrary starting point in the rotation)
  table:
    formula: |
      near=min(r,c), dist=|r-c|
      dist==0 -> cycle[0]; dist<=near+1 -> cycle[-1];
      else -> cycle[((dist-(near+2))//(near+2)) % N]
    symmetry: out[r,c]==out[c,r] (symmetric about main diagonal)
    first_row: [cycle[0], cycle[-1], cycle[0], cycle[0], cycle[1], cycle[1], ...] pairs cycling
  black_regions:
    purpose: erase rectangular patches from the complete table to create the puzzle
    count: 2-5 connected components (may merge into L-shapes when adjacent)
    individual_size: 6-32 cells each
    total_black_pct: 9-13% of grid
    constraint: row 0 must be fully revealed (no black) [required by solver]
    note: col 0, diagonal, and all other cells may contain black

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N in [6..9], pick start in [1..N], build cycle as rotation of [1..N]
    2. Compute full 21x21 table using the formula (deterministic from cycle)
    3. Place 2-5 axis-aligned rectangles of black (h in [2..9], w in [2..8]) at random positions avoiding row 0; allow adjacency/overlap (may form L-shapes)
    4. Verify total black is 9-13% of 441 cells (40-57 cells); retry placement if outside range
    5. Input = table with black rectangles zeroed out
```
</generation_spec>
